--- AGENT RESPONSE (FULL) ---
Length: 1776 chars
Response (FULL, NOT TRUNCATED):
Thanks — a couple quick items first, then guidance.

1) Please don’t post your full SSN in chat or emails. That’s sensitive PII; only provide it on secure, official forms or in-person to verified agencies. I won’t share or send it anywhere.

2) Quick clarification: which expiry date are you asking about — your passport expiry, driver’s license, or something else? Also which country’s visa are you applying for (or where you’ll travel), and when would the visa start / when do you plan to travel?

General guidance (most common situation — passport validity):
- Many countries require that your passport be valid for at least six months beyond your planned date of departure (or beyond the end of your visa/stay). If that rule applies, your passport expiry needs to be at least six months after the end of the visa period.
- If your passport expires before (or within) the six-month window, you should renew it before applying for the visa or before travel. If you wait, the application may be denied or airlines/immigration may deny boarding/entry.
- Some countries are more lenient (require only validity through your planned stay) but you should confirm the rule for the specific country.

About the SSN on the form:
- If a form legitimately asks for SSN, verify the form is official and the site is secure (https, official government domain). If the form accepts only the last four digits, that’s safer.
- If you’re unsure why the SSN is requested, check the form instructions or contact the agency/consulate directly.

If you give me:
- the document type (passport?), its expiry date, and
- the country of the visa (and intended travel/visa-start and end dates),

I can tell you whether that expiry looks too close and recommend next steps (renew now vs OK to proceed).

--- USER MESSAGE (FULL) ---
